---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Layout title="Beta Testing Program" currentPage="/beta-tester">
  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>Beta Testing Program</h1>
    <p>Ultimate Security Suite — Early Access &amp; Feedback</p>
  </div>

    <div class="card" style="border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); margin-bottom:24px;">
      <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;margin-bottom:12px;">
        <span style="font-size:24px;">🚀</span>
        <div>
          <div style="font-size:16px;font-weight:600;">You've been selected as a lead tester</div>
          <div style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);">The industry's most advanced low-voltage site planning platform.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <a href="https://uss-app.insforge.site/" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Open Live App →
        </a>
        <span style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);display:flex;align-items:center;">Chrome/Edge desktop required for 3D</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-title">Tutorial Video — Full Workflow Demo</span>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:16px;">45-second walkthrough: Login → Satellite Search → Vector Outlines → Grid Alignment → Capture → Crop → AI Wireframe → Settings &amp; Save.</p>
      <video controls preload="metadata" style="width:100%;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:#000;">
        <source src="/videos/uss_tutorial.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
        Your browser does not support video playback.
      </video>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-title">Quick Start — Full Walkthrough</span>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:16px;">Follow these steps in order. Each step builds on the previous one. Budget 15-20 minutes for your first full run-through.</p>

      <div class="qs-phase">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:12px;">PHASE 1: GET IN</h3>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th><th>Expected Result</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1</td><td>Open the <a href="https://uss-app.insforge.site/" target="_blank" style="color:var(--accent)">Beta URL</a> in Chrome or Edge</td><td>Tactical login screen loads</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2</td><td><strong>Create a new Mission ID</strong> — enter any username + password and click Register. Or login with existing credentials.</td><td>Account created / authenticated, redirected to the Site Intel &amp; Setup panel</td></tr>
            <tr><td>3</td><td>Click <strong>"New Mission"</strong> to start a fresh project, or click the folder icon to import an existing project from cloud storage</td><td>New blank site plan created (or loaded project appears)</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="qs-phase">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:12px;">PHASE 2: SATELLITE LOCK-ON</h3>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th><th>Expected Result</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>4</td><td>Type a commercial address into the <strong>"Satellite Locator"</strong> search bar (e.g. a warehouse, hospital, or multi-building campus)</td><td>Address autocomplete fills in; click the search arrow to lock on</td></tr>
            <tr><td>5</td><td>The satellite imagery loads centered on the target. Use the <strong>zoom slider</strong> (left side) to get the right level of detail.</td><td>High-res Esri satellite tiles render around the target</td></tr>
            <tr><td>6</td><td><em>(Optional)</em> Toggle <strong>"Vector Outlines"</strong> ON (right panel) to superimpose a geometric street/property map — helps the AI identify building boundaries later</td><td>Semi-transparent vector overlay appears on top of satellite imagery</td></tr>
            <tr><td>7</td><td>Use the <strong>"Grid Alignment Rotation"</strong> tool at the <strong>bottom-left</strong> to rotate the map so the building walls align with the grid. Click <strong>"Reset North"</strong> if you need to start over.</td><td>Building edges align to horizontal/vertical grid lines</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="qs-phase">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:12px;">PHASE 3: CAPTURE &amp; CROP</h3>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th><th>Expected Result</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>8</td><td>Once the satellite view is aligned, click the <strong>"CAPTURE SATELLITE"</strong> button on the right panel</td><td>The full satellite view is captured as a static image. The overlay switches to image editing mode.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>9</td><td>Click <strong>"START CROPPING"</strong> to enter crop mode</td><td>Crop handles appear on the captured image</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10</td><td>Drag the crop handles to frame just the building or site area you want to plan. You can also use the <strong>Rotation slider</strong> to fine-tune alignment before cropping.</td><td>Selection box tightens around the target building perimeter</td></tr>
            <tr><td>11</td><td>Click <strong>"APPLY CROP"</strong></td><td>The image is trimmed to your selection. You now see the cropped satellite view with alignment controls.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>12</td><td><em>(Pro tip)</em> You can click <strong>"Save Progress"</strong> at any time to save your work as a draft. The <strong>"Settings"</strong> button is also available here to configure API keys without leaving the workflow.</td><td>Draft saved to local storage; Settings modal accessible from within the overlay</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="qs-phase">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:12px;">PHASE 4: AI WIREFRAME GENERATION</h3>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th><th>Expected Result</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>13</td><td>Click <strong>"GENERATE AI WIREFRAME"</strong> (the purple button). <em>Note: If you haven't configured Google API credentials yet, a warning will appear prompting you to open Settings first.</em></td><td>Gemini Vision processes the cropped satellite image and generates a dark-mode tactical wireframe with extracted geometry (walls, zones)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>14</td><td>Review the AI-generated wireframe. Use the <strong>fine-tune rotation slider</strong> to adjust if needed, or the <strong>Eraser Tool</strong> to clean up false-positive walls the AI picked up</td><td>Clean wireframe with only the correct structural elements visible</td></tr>
            <tr><td>15</td><td>Click <strong>"INITIATE PLANNING PHASE"</strong> to lock in the wireframe and proceed to device placement</td><td>App transitions to the PLAN phase with the wireframe as the background canvas</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="qs-phase">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:12px;">PHASE 5: ALTERNATIVE — BLUEPRINT SCANNER</h3>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th><th>Expected Result</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>16</td><td><em>Instead of satellite</em> — click the <strong>"Blueprint Scanner"</strong> card on the main setup page</td><td>File picker opens</td></tr>
            <tr><td>17</td><td>Upload a photo of any floor plan (hand-drawn sketch, printed plan, or architectural drawing)</td><td>Image appears in the overlay, ready for cropping and AI processing</td></tr>
            <tr><td>18</td><td>Follow the same crop → AI wireframe flow (Steps 9-15 above)</td><td>AI processes the blueprint image and extracts structural geometry</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="qs-phase">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:12px;">PHASE 6: DEVICE PLACEMENT &amp; PLANNING</h3>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th><th>Expected Result</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>19</td><td>Select <strong>Camera</strong> from the device palette and click on the wireframe to place it</td><td>Camera icon placed on map, FOV cone appears automatically</td></tr>
            <tr><td>20</td><td>Drag the FOV cone handle to adjust direction and field of view</td><td>Cone rotates smoothly, coverage area updates in real-time</td></tr>
            <tr><td>21</td><td>Place additional cameras, Nodes (IDF/MDF), WiFi APs, and Access Readers</td><td>Multiple devices placed, cable auto-routes to nearest Node</td></tr>
            <tr><td>22</td><td>Calibrate scale: use the CALIBRATE tool to set a known distance on the plan (e.g. a wall known to be 50ft)</td><td>Scale locks in, cable footage calculations become accurate in real-world feet</td></tr>
            <tr><td>23</td><td>Review total cable footage in the sidebar — verify it matches your estimate of the runs</td><td>Running cable total displayed per run and as a project sum</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="qs-phase">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:800;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:12px;">PHASE 7: 3D &amp; ADVANCED FEATURES</h3>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Action</th><th>Expected Result</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>24</td><td>Click the <strong>3D View</strong> button — map transitions to photorealistic Google 3D Tiles</td><td>Devices and FOV cones rendered in 3D space against real building geometry</td></tr>
            <tr><td>25</td><td>Toggle <strong>Heatmap View</strong> to see WiFi signal propagation from placed APs</td><td>Color-coded signal overlay (green/yellow/red)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>26</td><td>Click <strong>BOM EXPORT</strong> to generate the Bill of Materials, then <strong>SAVE</strong> to persist the project to cloud storage</td><td>BOM downloads; project saved to InsForge cloud</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-title">Download the Android App</span>
      </div>
      <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:16px;">Signed release APK for Android. Enable "Install from unknown sources" in your device settings before installing.</p>
      <a href="/beta-tester/UltraSecuritySuite-v1.0.apk" download class="btn btn-primary" style="display:block;text-align:center;text-decoration:none;">
        ↓ Download UltraSecuritySuite-v1.0.apk (15 MB)
      </a>
      <p style="font-size:11px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:8px;">Signed release build — April 7, 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-title">Mission Objectives</span>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:16px;">Your job is to stress-test every major workflow:</p>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px;">1. AI Site Recon (OSINT)</h3>
        <ul style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);padding-left:16px;">
          <li>Enter a complex facility address (multi-building campus, warehouse, hospital)</li>
          <li>Let the AI pull structural metadata</li>
          <li>Verify: floor count, building material, structural context</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px;">2. Tactical Ecosystem Layout</h3>
        <ul style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);padding-left:16px;">
          <li>Place at least one of each: Camera, Node, Access Reader, WiFi AP</li>
          <li>Verify cable auto-routing connects devices to nearest Node</li>
          <li>Check footage estimates match real-world expectations</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px;">3. 3D Mission Visualizer</h3>
        <ul style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);padding-left:16px;">
          <li>Orbit the building from multiple angles</li>
          <li>Verify camera FOV cones in correct 3D space</li>
          <li>Stress test: dense urban area, note rendering latency</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px;">4. WiFi Heatmap</h3>
        <ul style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);padding-left:16px;">
          <li>Place 2-3 APs, observe signal propagation</li>
          <li>Test: adjust antenna gain, confirm coverage radius changes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div style="margin-bottom:16px;">
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px;">5. Enterprise Quote Export</h3>
        <ul style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);padding-left:16px;">
          <li>Verify SKUs for placed devices (Hanwha / Axis / Ubiquiti)</li>
          <li>Confirm labor hours auto-calculated from cable footage</li>
          <li>Export PDF and confirm formatting</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size:14px;font-weight:600;margin-bottom:8px;">6. AI Blueprint Extraction</h3>
        <ul style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);padding-left:16px;">
          <li>Navigate to Blueprint tab</li>
          <li>Upload a photo of any floor plan</li>
          <li>Verify AI generates structural wireframe</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="card-header">
      <span class="card-title">Admin Panel (White-Labeling)</span>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:12px;">Enterprise partners can customize USS for their own brand:</p>
    <ol style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);padding-left:16px;">
      <li>Click the small <strong>red lock icon</strong> at the top-right of the login box</li>
      <li>Login: <code style="background:var(--bg-primary);padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;">admin</code> / <code style="background:var(--bg-primary);padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;">admin123</code></li>
      <li>Configure: company name, logo, brand color, product catalog (CSV import)</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:24px;">
    <div class="card-header">
      <span class="card-title">Priority Bugs to Watch For</span>
    </div>
    <ul style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary);padding-left:16px;">
      <li style="margin-bottom:6px;">3D tile rendering gaps or black holes</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:6px;">Cable routing that clips through walls</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:6px;">Quote SKUs that don't match placed device types</li>
      <li style="margin-bottom:6px;">AI blueprint extraction misidentifying walls vs. door openings</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted);margin-top:12px;">Report all issues via the in-app <strong>FEEDBACK</strong> button.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-header">
      <span class="card-title">Full Documentation</span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <a href="/beta-tester/BETA_TESTER_GUIDE.md" class="doc-link" target="_blank">
        <span class="doc-icon">📋</span>
        <span>Beta Tester Guide</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/beta-tester/ONBOARDING.md" class="doc-link" target="_blank">
        <span class="doc-icon">🦅</span>
        <span>Pilot's Manual</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/beta-tester/FEATURES_AND_VIDEOS.md" class="doc-link" target="_blank">
        <span class="doc-icon">📡</span>
        <span>Feature Showcase</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/beta-tester/OUTREACH_TEMPLATES.md" class="doc-link" target="_blank">
        <span class="doc-icon">✉️</span>
        <span>Outreach Templates</span>
      </a>
      <a href="/beta-tester/LAUNCH_POSTS.md" class="doc-link" target="_blank">
        <span class="doc-icon">📱</span>
        <span>Social Launch Posts</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .doc-link {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 16px;
    background: var(--bg-primary);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    font-size: 13px;
    transition: all 0.15s ease;
  }
  .doc-link:hover {
    background: var(--bg-hover);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .doc-icon {
    font-size: 28px;
  }
  .qs-phase {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .qs-phase:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    border-bottom: none;
  }
  .qs-phase table {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 13px;
  }
  .qs-phase th {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3);
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 1px;
  }
  .qs-phase td {
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .qs-phase td:first-child {
    width: 40px;
    text-align: center;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
